[2026-03-14T21:47:03.221Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017DzrXQs7UMXGLW7UJXuzFM","type":"tool_result","content":"   750→### GroupBySort\n   751→\n   752→#### Test: Group by control renders with default \"Status\" selected\n   753→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues page\n   754→- **Expected**: A \"Group by\" control/dropdown is visible in the toolbar area. It shows \"Status\" as the currently selected grouping option.\n   755→\n   756→#### Test: Group by dropdown shows all grouping options\n   757→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues page\n   758→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Group by\" control\n   759→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing options: Status, Priority, Assignee, Project, Label, None. Each option is clickable.\n   760→\n   761→#### Test: Group by Priority groups issues under priority headers\n   762→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues with priorities: Urgent (1), High (2), Medium (1), Low (1), No Priority (1)\n   763→- **Action**: User selects \"Priority\" from the Group by dropdown\n   764→- **Expected**: Issues are regrouped under priority headers: Urgent, High, Medium, Low, No Priority. Each header shows the priority icon, name, and count. Empty priority groups are not shown.\n   765→\n   766→#### Test: Group by Assignee groups issues under assignee headers\n   767→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues assigned to Alice (2), Bob (1), and unassigned (1)\n   768→- **Action**: User selects \"Assignee\" from the Group by dropdown\n   769→- **Expected**: Issues are grouped under assignee name headers with their avatars. An \"Unassigned\" group shows issues with no assignee. Each header shows the assignee avatar, name, and issue count.\n   770→\n   771→#### Test: Group by Project groups issues under project headers\n   772→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues in project \"Auth Rewrite\" (2), \"Dashboard v2\" (1), and no project (1)\n   773→- **Action**: User selects \"Project\" from the Group by dropdown\n   774→- **Expected**: Issues are grouped under project name headers. A \"No Project\" group shows unassigned issues. Each header shows the project name and issue count.\n   775→\n   776→#### Test: Group by Label groups issues under label headers\n   777→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues with labels \"Bug\" (2), \"Feature\" (1), and no labels (1)\n   778→- **Action**: User selects \"Label\" from the Group by dropdown\n   779→- **Expected**: Issues are grouped under label name headers with colored dots. A \"No Label\" group shows unlabeled issues. Issues with multiple labels appear under each applicable label group.\n   780→\n   781→#### Test: Group by None shows a flat list\n   782→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has 6 issues in various statuses\n   783→- **Action**: User selects \"None\" from the Group by dropdown\n   784→- **Expected**: All issues are displayed in a flat list without any group headers. Issues are shown in the current sort order.\n   785→\n   786→#### Test: Switching group by option re-renders immediately\n   787→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issues are grouped by Status\n   788→- **Action**: User changes Group by from \"Status\" to \"Priority\"\n   789→- **Expected**: The issue list immediately re-renders with priority-based grouping. No page reload is needed. The transition is smooth.\n   790→\n   791→#### Test: Group by can be changed multiple times\n   792→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues\n   793→- **Action**: User selects \"Priority\" grouping, then \"Assignee\", then back to \"Status\"\n   794→- **Expected**: Each change correctly re-groups the issues. After returning to \"Status\", the view matches the original default grouping.\n   795→\n   796→#### Test: Sort by control renders with default option\n   797→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues page\n   798→- **Expected**: A \"Sort by\" control/dropdown is visible in the toolbar area, showing the current sort option.\n   799→\n   800→#### Test: Sort by dropdown shows all sorting options\n   801→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues page\n   802→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Sort by\" control\n   803→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing options: Priority, Created date, Updated date, Status. Each option is clickable.\n   804→\n   805→#### Test: Sort by Priority orders issues by priority level\n   806→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues with mixed priorities within status groups\n   807→- **Action**: User selects \"Priority\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   808→- **Expected**: Within each group, issues are ordered by priority: Urgent first, then High, Medium, Low, No Priority last.\n   809→\n   810→#### Test: Sort by Created date orders issues by creation time\n   811→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues created at different times\n   812→- **Action**: User selects \"Created date\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   813→- **Expected**: Within each group, issues are ordered by creation date (newest first).\n   814→\n   815→#### Test: Sort by Updated date orders issues by last update time\n   816→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues updated at different times\n   817→- **Action**: User selects \"Updated date\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   818→- **Expected**: Within each group, issues are ordered by last update time (most recently updated first).\n   819→\n   820→#### Test: Sort by Status orders issues by status progression\n   821→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, group by is set to \"None\" (flat list)\n   822→- **Action**: User selects \"Status\" from the Sort by dropdown\n   823→- **Expected**: Issues are ordered by status progression: Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled.\n   824→\n   825→#### Test: Sort works correctly within groups\n   826→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, grouped by Status, \"In Progress\" group has 3 issues with different priorities\n   827→- **Action**: User selects \"Priority\" from Sort by\n   828→- **Expected**: The 3 issues within the \"In Progress\" group are reordered by priority (Urgent first, No Priority last). Other groups are similarly sorted.\n   829→\n   830→#### Test: Sort by can be changed multiple times\n   831→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues\n   832→- **Action**: User sorts by \"Priority\", then by \"Created date\", then by \"Updated date\"\n   833→- **Expected**: Each sort change correctly reorders issues within their groups. The sort control updates to reflect the current selection.\n   834→\n   835→### TeamFilters\n   836→\n   837→#### Test: Team filters toolbar renders with all filter options\n   838→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/team/eng-1/issues`\n   839→- **Expected**: A toolbar at the top of the issue list displays filter controls: \"Status\", \"Priority\", \"Assignee\", \"Label\", \"Project\", and \"Cycle\" filters. Each shows as a button/chip that can be clicked to open a dropdown.\n   840→\n   841→#### Test: Status filter dropdown shows all statuses with icons\n   842→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues\n   843→- **Action**: User clicks the \"Status\" filter button\n   844→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing all statuses: Backlog (dotted circle, gray), Todo (circle, gray), In Progress (half circle, yellow), In Review (three-quarter circle, blue), Done (check circle, green), Cancelled (x-circle, red). Each option has a checkbox.\n   845→\n   846→#### Test: Status filter filters issues by selected statuses\n   847→- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues in Backlog (3), In Progress (2), Done (1)\n   848→- **Action**: User opens the Status filter and selects only \"In Progress\"\n   849→- **Expected**: Only the \"In Progress\" group is displayed with its 2 issues. Backlog and Done groups are hidden. The Status filter button shows a visual indicator that a filter is active."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bfa44b73-8bd5-4621-8202-172b5d211566","uuid":"f7e7be31-cdbc-42fc-9e4f-a0336d68dd05","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/apps/LinearClone/docs/tests.md","content":"### GroupBySort\n\n#### Test: Group by control renders with default \"Status\" selected\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues page\n- **Expected**: A \"Group by\" control/dropdown is visible in the toolbar area. It shows \"Status\" as the currently selected grouping option.\n\n#### Test: Group by dropdown shows all grouping options\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues page\n- **Action**: User clicks the \"Group by\" control\n- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing options: Status, Priority, Assignee, Project, Label, None. Each option is clickable.\n\n#### Test: Group by Priority groups issues under priority headers\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues with priorities: Urgent (1), High (2), Medium (1), Low (1), No Priority (1)\n- **Action**: User selects \"Priority\" from the Group by dropdown\n- **Expected**: Issues are regrouped under priority headers: Urgent, High, Medium, Low, No Priority. Each header shows the priority icon, name, and count. Empty priority groups are not shown.\n\n#### Test: Group by Assignee groups issues under assignee headers\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues assigned to Alice (2), Bob (1), and unassigned (1)\n- **Action**: User selects \"Assignee\" from the Group by dropdown\n- **Expected**: Issues are grouped under assignee name headers with their avatars. An \"Unassigned\" group shows issues with no assignee. Each header shows the assignee avatar, name, and issue count.\n\n#### Test: Group by Project groups issues under project headers\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues in project \"Auth Rewrite\" (2), \"Dashboard v2\" (1), and no project (1)\n- **Action**: User selects \"Project\" from the Group by dropdown\n- **Expected**: Issues are grouped under project name headers. A \"No Project\" group shows unassigned issues. Each header shows the project name and issue count.\n\n#### Test: Group by Label groups issues under label headers\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues with labels \"Bug\" (2), \"Feature\" (1), and no labels (1)\n- **Action**: User selects \"Label\" from the Group by dropdown\n- **Expected**: Issues are grouped under label name headers with colored dots. A \"No Label\" group shows unlabeled issues. Issues with multiple labels appear under each applicable label group.\n\n#### Test: Group by None shows a flat list\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has 6 issues in various statuses\n- **Action**: User selects \"None\" from the Group by dropdown\n- **Expected**: All issues are displayed in a flat list without any group headers. Issues are shown in the current sort order.\n\n#### Test: Switching group by option re-renders immediately\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, issues are grouped by Status\n- **Action**: User changes Group by from \"Status\" to \"Priority\"\n- **Expected**: The issue list immediately re-renders with priority-based grouping. No page reload is needed. The transition is smooth.\n\n#### Test: Group by can be changed multiple times\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues\n- **Action**: User selects \"Priority\" grouping, then \"Assignee\", then back to \"Status\"\n- **Expected**: Each change correctly re-groups the issues. After returning to \"Status\", the view matches the original default grouping.\n\n#### Test: Sort by control renders with default option\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues page\n- **Expected**: A \"Sort by\" control/dropdown is visible in the toolbar area, showing the current sort option.\n\n#### Test: Sort by dropdown shows all sorting options\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues page\n- **Action**: User clicks the \"Sort by\" control\n- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing options: Priority, Created date, Updated date, Status. Each option is clickable.\n\n#### Test: Sort by Priority orders issues by priority level\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues with mixed priorities within status groups\n- **Action**: User selects \"Priority\" from the Sort by dropdown\n- **Expected**: Within each group, issues are ordered by priority: Urgent first, then High, Medium, Low, No Priority last.\n\n#### Test: Sort by Created date orders issues by creation time\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues created at different times\n- **Action**: User selects \"Created date\" from the Sort by dropdown\n- **Expected**: Within each group, issues are ordered by creation date (newest first).\n\n#### Test: Sort by Updated date orders issues by last update time\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues updated at different times\n- **Action**: User selects \"Updated date\" from the Sort by dropdown\n- **Expected**: Within each group, issues are ordered by last update time (most recently updated first).\n\n#### Test: Sort by Status orders issues by status progression\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, group by is set to \"None\" (flat list)\n- **Action**: User selects \"Status\" from the Sort by dropdown\n- **Expected**: Issues are ordered by status progression: Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled.\n\n#### Test: Sort works correctly within groups\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, grouped by Status, \"In Progress\" group has 3 issues with different priorities\n- **Action**: User selects \"Priority\" from Sort by\n- **Expected**: The 3 issues within the \"In Progress\" group are reordered by priority (Urgent first, No Priority last). Other groups are similarly sorted.\n\n#### Test: Sort by can be changed multiple times\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues\n- **Action**: User sorts by \"Priority\", then by \"Created date\", then by \"Updated date\"\n- **Expected**: Each sort change correctly reorders issues within their groups. The sort control updates to reflect the current selection.\n\n### TeamFilters\n\n#### Test: Team filters toolbar renders with all filter options\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing `/team/eng-1/issues`\n- **Expected**: A toolbar at the top of the issue list displays filter controls: \"Status\", \"Priority\", \"Assignee\", \"Label\", \"Project\", and \"Cycle\" filters. Each shows as a button/chip that can be clicked to open a dropdown.\n\n#### Test: Status filter dropdown shows all statuses with icons\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, viewing team issues\n- **Action**: User clicks the \"Status\" filter button\n- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown opens showing all statuses: Backlog (dotted circle, gray), Todo (circle, gray), In Progress (half circle, yellow), In Review (three-quarter circle, blue), Done (check circle, green), Cancelled (x-circle, red). Each option has a checkbox.\n\n#### Test: Status filter filters issues by selected statuses\n- **Initial state**: User is authenticated, team has issues in Backlog (3), In Progress (2), Done (1)\n- **Action**: User opens the Status filter and selects only \"In Progress\"\n- **Expected**: Only the \"In Progress\" group is displayed with its 2 issues. Backlog and Done groups are hidden. The Status filter button shows a visual indicator that a filter is active.","numLines":100,"startLine":750,"totalLines":2686}}}
