[2026-03-14T21:47:32.544Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014kn77MzCnhjhxHh8Qc613G","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I now have a comprehensive understanding of the testing patterns. Let me provide you with a summary of the testing setup and patterns:\n\n## Testing Patterns Summary for LinearClone\n\n### 1. **Playwright Configuration** (`playwright.config.ts`)\n- **Test Directory**: `./tests`\n- **Timeout**: 60 seconds per test, 10 seconds for assertions\n- **Parallelization**: Tests run in parallel (`fullyParallel: true`)\n- **Retries**: 0 (no automatic retries)\n- **Base URL**: `http://localhost:8888`\n- **Reporters**: Replay reporter, JSON results, and HTML report\n- **Recording**: Uses Replay Chromium device for debugging\n\n### 2. **Common Authentication & Setup Pattern**\n\nTests follow a consistent pattern for login and API interaction:\n\n```typescript\n// API Login Helper\nasync function loginViaApi(baseURL: string, email: string, password: string) {\n  const response = await fetch(`${baseURL}/api/login`, {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    body: JSON.stringify({ email, password }),\n  });\n  return response.json(); // Returns { token, user, ... }\n}\n\n// Store token in localStorage\nawait page.evaluate((t) => localStorage.setItem('session_token', t), token);\n```\n\n### 3. **Navigation & Page Readiness Pattern**\n\nTests use consistent waits for page visibility:\n```typescript\n// Navigate and wait for page indicator\nawait page.goto('/my-issues');\nawait expect(page.getByTestId('my-issues-page')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 });\n```\n\n### 4. **Test Structure**\n\nEach spec file follows this pattern:\n- Import `test, expect` from `@playwright/test`\n- Define helper functions at the top (login, navigation, API calls)\n- Use `test.describe()` for grouping related tests\n- Each test is a single `test()` call with descriptive name\n\n### 5. **Shared Helper Functions Across Tests**\n\n**loginViaApi(baseURL, email, password)**\n- Makes POST request to `/api/login`\n- Returns token and user data\n- Used in almost every test\n\n**getTeams(baseURL, token)**\n- Fetches available teams via API\n- Filters by team identifier (e.g., 'ENG')\n- Returns teams array\n\n**loginAndNavigateToTeamIssues(page, baseURL, email, password)**\n- Combines API login, localStorage setup, and navigation\n- Returns `{ token, user, engTeam }`\n- Common in team-related tests\n\n**getTeamIssues(baseURL, token, teamId)**\n- Fetches issues for a specific team via API\n\n**createIssueViaApi(baseURL, token, issueData)**\n- Creates issue with: teamId, title, status, priority, assigneeId\n- Used for dynamic test data\n\n**createTestUser(baseURL, name, email, password)**\n- Calls `/api/signup` to create test users\n- Used for multi-user scenarios\n\n### 6. **Test Data Selectors (testid Pattern)**\n\nAll tests rely on `data-testid` attributes following patterns like:\n- `{page-type}-page`: e.g., `my-issues-page`, `team-issues-page`\n- `{item}-row-{id}`: e.g., `issue-row-ENG-1`\n- `{field}-{status}`: e.g., `team-issue-group-header-backlog`\n- `{element}-{id}`: e.g., `issue-identifier-${eng1.id}`, `issue-priority-${eng1.id}`\n\n### 7. **Assertion Patterns**\n\nTests use consistent Playwright assertions:\n```typescript\nawait expect(page.getByTestId('...')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 });\nawait expect(page.getByTestId('...')).toContainText('...');\nawait expect(page.getByTestId('...')).toHaveText('...');\nawait expect(page.getByTestId('...')).toHaveCount(n);\nawait expect(page.getByTestId('...')).toHaveAttribute('attr', 'value');\nawait expect(page).toHaveURL('/path');\n```\n\n### 8. **Common Test Scenarios**\n\n- **List rendering**: Verify groups with correct counts\n- **Visual ordering**: Use `boundingBox()` to verify element positioning\n- **User interactions**: Click, select dropdown, verify state changes\n- **API-driven tests**: Create data via API, verify UI reflection\n- **Empty states**: Test behavior with no data\n- **Multiple groups/filters**: Test independent state management\n\n### 9. **File Organization**\n\nTest files in `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/` directory:\n- `team-issues.spec.ts` - Team issues list tests\n- `team-issues-row.spec.ts` - Issue row component tests\n- `my-issues.spec.ts` - Personal issues list tests\n- `login.spec.ts`, `signup.spec.ts` - Auth tests\n- `sidebar*.spec.ts` - Navigation tests\n- `*-bulk-actions.spec.ts` - Multi-select operations\n\n### 10. **Key Testing Patterns to Follow**\n\n1. Always use `{ timeout: 30000 }` for initial page visibility waits\n2. Use API calls for test data setup (cleaner than UI interactions)\n3. Store login token in localStorage before navigating to authenticated pages\n4. Group related tests with `test.describe()`\n5. Use `data-testid` selectors exclusively (no CSS selectors in most cases)\n6. Verify UI state changes after API-driven modifications\n7. Test both \"happy path\" and edge cases (empty states, multiple interactions)\n8. Use specific identifiers (`eng1.id`) when clicking specific elements\n\nAll the test files are located in `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/` and follow these consistent patterns throughout the codebase."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a1d0a01bae226c024 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 34611\ntool_uses: 9\nduration_ms: 18962</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bfa44b73-8bd5-4621-8202-172b5d211566","uuid":"ba0fdfdd-d949-49bd-b238-db1217b3f5e0","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /repo/apps/LinearClone, read:\n1. The playwright.config.ts file\n2. One or two existing spec files (e.g., team-issues.spec.ts, my-issues.spec.ts) to understand the test patterns, imports, authentication setup, and how tests are structured\n3. Any test fixtures or helpers used\n\nI need to understand the testing patterns so I can write new tests consistently.","agentId":"a1d0a01bae226c024","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I now have a comprehensive understanding of the testing patterns. Let me provide you with a summary of the testing setup and patterns:\n\n## Testing Patterns Summary for LinearClone\n\n### 1. **Playwright Configuration** (`playwright.config.ts`)\n- **Test Directory**: `./tests`\n- **Timeout**: 60 seconds per test, 10 seconds for assertions\n- **Parallelization**: Tests run in parallel (`fullyParallel: true`)\n- **Retries**: 0 (no automatic retries)\n- **Base URL**: `http://localhost:8888`\n- **Reporters**: Replay reporter, JSON results, and HTML report\n- **Recording**: Uses Replay Chromium device for debugging\n\n### 2. **Common Authentication & Setup Pattern**\n\nTests follow a consistent pattern for login and API interaction:\n\n```typescript\n// API Login Helper\nasync function loginViaApi(baseURL: string, email: string, password: string) {\n  const response = await fetch(`${baseURL}/api/login`, {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    body: JSON.stringify({ email, password }),\n  });\n  return response.json(); // Returns { token, user, ... }\n}\n\n// Store token in localStorage\nawait page.evaluate((t) => localStorage.setItem('session_token', t), token);\n```\n\n### 3. **Navigation & Page Readiness Pattern**\n\nTests use consistent waits for page visibility:\n```typescript\n// Navigate and wait for page indicator\nawait page.goto('/my-issues');\nawait expect(page.getByTestId('my-issues-page')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 });\n```\n\n### 4. **Test Structure**\n\nEach spec file follows this pattern:\n- Import `test, expect` from `@playwright/test`\n- Define helper functions at the top (login, navigation, API calls)\n- Use `test.describe()` for grouping related tests\n- Each test is a single `test()` call with descriptive name\n\n### 5. **Shared Helper Functions Across Tests**\n\n**loginViaApi(baseURL, email, password)**\n- Makes POST request to `/api/login`\n- Returns token and user data\n- Used in almost every test\n\n**getTeams(baseURL, token)**\n- Fetches available teams via API\n- Filters by team identifier (e.g., 'ENG')\n- Returns teams array\n\n**loginAndNavigateToTeamIssues(page, baseURL, email, password)**\n- Combines API login, localStorage setup, and navigation\n- Returns `{ token, user, engTeam }`\n- Common in team-related tests\n\n**getTeamIssues(baseURL, token, teamId)**\n- Fetches issues for a specific team via API\n\n**createIssueViaApi(baseURL, token, issueData)**\n- Creates issue with: teamId, title, status, priority, assigneeId\n- Used for dynamic test data\n\n**createTestUser(baseURL, name, email, password)**\n- Calls `/api/signup` to create test users\n- Used for multi-user scenarios\n\n### 6. **Test Data Selectors (testid Pattern)**\n\nAll tests rely on `data-testid` attributes following patterns like:\n- `{page-type}-page`: e.g., `my-issues-page`, `team-issues-page`\n- `{item}-row-{id}`: e.g., `issue-row-ENG-1`\n- `{field}-{status}`: e.g., `team-issue-group-header-backlog`\n- `{element}-{id}`: e.g., `issue-identifier-${eng1.id}`, `issue-priority-${eng1.id}`\n\n### 7. **Assertion Patterns**\n\nTests use consistent Playwright assertions:\n```typescript\nawait expect(page.getByTestId('...')).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 });\nawait expect(page.getByTestId('...')).toContainText('...');\nawait expect(page.getByTestId('...')).toHaveText('...');\nawait expect(page.getByTestId('...')).toHaveCount(n);\nawait expect(page.getByTestId('...')).toHaveAttribute('attr', 'value');\nawait expect(page).toHaveURL('/path');\n```\n\n### 8. **Common Test Scenarios**\n\n- **List rendering**: Verify groups with correct counts\n- **Visual ordering**: Use `boundingBox()` to verify element positioning\n- **User interactions**: Click, select dropdown, verify state changes\n- **API-driven tests**: Create data via API, verify UI reflection\n- **Empty states**: Test behavior with no data\n- **Multiple groups/filters**: Test independent state management\n\n### 9. **File Organization**\n\nTest files in `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/` directory:\n- `team-issues.spec.ts` - Team issues list tests\n- `team-issues-row.spec.ts` - Issue row component tests\n- `my-issues.spec.ts` - Personal issues list tests\n- `login.spec.ts`, `signup.spec.ts` - Auth tests\n- `sidebar*.spec.ts` - Navigation tests\n- `*-bulk-actions.spec.ts` - Multi-select operations\n\n### 10. **Key Testing Patterns to Follow**\n\n1. Always use `{ timeout: 30000 }` for initial page visibility waits\n2. Use API calls for test data setup (cleaner than UI interactions)\n3. Store login token in localStorage before navigating to authenticated pages\n4. Group related tests with `test.describe()`\n5. Use `data-testid` selectors exclusively (no CSS selectors in most cases)\n6. Verify UI state changes after API-driven modifications\n7. Test both \"happy path\" and edge cases (empty states, multiple interactions)\n8. Use specific identifiers (`eng1.id`) when clicking specific elements\n\nAll the test files are located in `/repo/apps/LinearClone/tests/` and follow these consistent patterns throughout the codebase."}],"totalDurationMs":18962,"totalTokens":34611,"totalToolUseCount":9,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5820,"cache_read_input_tokens":27346,"output_tokens":1439,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5820},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
